  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "If $\\mathrm{C}$ be $(\\mathrm{h}, \\mathrm{k})$ then centroid is $(\\mathrm{h} / 3,(\\mathrm{k}-2) / 3)$ it lies on $2 x+3 y=1$. $\\Rightarrow$ locus is $2 x+3 y=9$",
    "image": null
